  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Management and Training has recorded $281M in contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Management and Training won 35 awards this fiscal year to date, with an average award size of $8M. Management and Training obligations are up 33.6% year over year. Management and Training obligations peaked at $382M in FY21 and then declined through FY25 before rising to $281M in FY26. Management and Training receives the bulk of FY2026 obligations from the Department of Labor, which obligated $248M, followed by the Department of Homeland Security, which obligated $33.1M. Management and Training work in the Other Technical and Trade Schools market, which accounts for $248M, and in Security Guards and Patrol Services, which accounts for $33.1M. The figures shown reflect contract obligations except where tables list award values or expiring-contract totals as noted on the page.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Management and Training's contract activity changed year over year?",
        "body": "Management and Training obligations are up 33.6% year over year. Management and Training recorded $281M in FY26 to date after obligations of $211M in FY25 and $234M in FY24. Management and Training obligations were $259M in FY23, $267M in FY22, and $382M in FY21."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top buyers and what markets does Management and Training serve?",
        "body": "The Department of Labor is the top buyer for Management and Training, with $248M in obligations in FY2026 to date. The Department of Homeland Security follows with $33.1M in obligations. Management and Training serves the Other Technical and Trade Schools market at $248M and the Security Guards and Patrol Services market at $33.1M."
      }
    ]
  },
